## Setup and render

Requires Quarto, a working LaTeX installation, and Make. Install the project-local [coatless-quarto/assign](https://github.com/coatless-quarto/assign) extension once (and commit `_extensions/` for reproducibility):

```sh
make setup
make exams            # assignment, solution, grading PDFs
make exams-assign
make exams-solution
make exams-grading
```

Output goes to `_output/assignment`, `_output/solution`, and `_output/grading`. This is a **default document project**, not a website.

Author the exam in `exam.qmd`. Keep reusable question content in `tasks/*.qmd` and include it with Quarto's `{% raw %}{{< include tasks/example.qmd >}}{% endraw %}` shortcode, as demonstrated in `exam.qmd`. Each task can contain common text and `:::{.direction}`, `:::{.sol}`, `:::{.rubric}` sections; the extension selects the content for each profile. Keep points in `exam.qmd`, not in reusable tasks. The cover sheet lives in `partials/before-body.tex` and is shown only in the assignment profile.

**Important:** The initial question count and total points populate the cover sheet at generation time. If you change them after generation, update `partials/before-body.tex` as well. Complete the question headings and possible-points row to match the actual exam.

